cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its data, please cite the paper below."
title: "conv-vs-ped-tutor: a controlled tutor-agent experiment on conversational vs. pedagogical alignment"
abstract: >-
  Code, algebra problems, and results for a comparison of conversational and
  pedagogical tutoring policies across three language models. Two LLM judges rated
  the same tutor turns for helpfulness and pedagogy. The study also measured
  answer disclosure and independent work by a simulated student.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/bydeng01/conv-vs-ped-tutor"
keywords:
  - LLM-as-a-judge
  - intelligent tutoring systems
  - pedagogical alignment
  - pre-registration
  - reproducibility
